      "body": "<!-- devin-review-comment {\"id\": \"BUG_pr-review-job-a6c016f64bc442f5b9dd5c204451e00c_0001\", \"file_path\": \"recall-backend/index.ts\", \"start_line\": 444, \"end_line\": 444, \"side\": \"RIGHT\", \"based_on_repo_rules\": false, \"kind\": \"bug\"} -->\n\n🟡 **Chat citations disappear across deployments**\n\nWhen the backend deploys first, `sources` leaves existing frontend tabs without clickable citations. The old parser accepts only `citations`; the new parser also ignores older backend events.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Learn more</summary>\n\nThe API server and frontend deploy separately, and an already-open browser tab keeps running its old frontend bundle. That bundle only recognizes a `citations` event, so it ignores the newly named `sources` event even though it still displays streamed text. Deploying the frontend first causes the reverse mismatch: the new parser ignores an older server's `citations` event. Both versions need to overlap during a release.\n\n**Example:** A user opens Ask AI before a Railway backend update, then asks a question afterward. The server sends `sources`, but the existing tab ignores it and renders `[1]` without a link.\n\n**Recommended fix:** Preserve a compatibility path on both ends: let the new parser accept `citations` and `sources`, and have the backend emit the old event alongside the new one until older tabs have aged out. Keep event order before streamed text so either client can link citations.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- devin-review-badge-begin -->\n<a href=\"https://app.devin.ai/review/sunnybagal/recall-seeded/pull/1\" target=\"_blank\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-dark.svg?v=4\"><img src=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-light.svg?v=4\" alt=\"Devin Review\"></picture></a>\n<!-- devin-review-badge-end -->\n\n---\n*Was this helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to provide feedback.*",
